WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:17.895
On my first day of freedom, I went into the capital city, Mildendo.

2
00:00:17.896 --> 00:00:22.232
I stepped over the city walls and walked through the streets.

3
00:00:22.233 --> 00:00:27.218
Most of the houses in Mildendo had three to five stories.

4
00:00:27.219 --> 00:00:34.145
They were painted in many bright colors, and some had unusual patterns painted on them.

5
00:00:34.146 --> 00:00:38.090
People watched me curiously from every window.

6
00:00:38.091 --> 00:00:43.600
The city was a square, with two main streets that crossed in the middle of the city.

7
00:00:43.601 --> 00:00:47.789
These two streets divided Mildendo into quarters.

8
00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:52.912
The main streets were just wide enough for me to walk down.

9
00:00:52.913 --> 00:01:00.729
I could not go into the smaller streets, though, because my feet were too big and those streets were too narrow.

10
00:01:00.730 --> 00:01:09.770
Because the Lilliputians are so small, I had to walk very carefully so as not to step on anyone.

11
00:01:09.771 --> 00:01:13.998
"Hello!" I said to people as I passed them.

12
00:01:13.999 --> 00:01:15.963
Some people waved.

13
00:01:15.964 --> 00:01:21.269
A man in a blue coat called out, "Welcome to Mildendo."

14
00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:26.141
"This is the most crowded city I've ever seen," I said to him.

15
00:01:26.142 --> 00:01:31.669
"Five hundred thousand people live here," he replied almost proudly.

16
00:01:31.670 --> 00:01:38.424
The king's palace was in the center of the city, surrounded by a high, thick wall.

17
00:01:38.425 --> 00:01:42.557
I climbed over the wall and lay down on the ground.

18
00:01:42.558 --> 00:01:46.333
From there I could see into the palace rooms.

19
00:01:46.334 --> 00:01:51.446
Everything in the palace was beautiful, just as the king had said.

20
00:01:51.447 --> 00:01:56.050
In one room I saw the queen talking with some ladies.

21
00:01:56.051 --> 00:01:59.854
When she saw me, she came to the window.

22
00:01:59.855 --> 00:02:05.733
"Enormous One," she said, "welcome to our fair city.

23
00:02:05.734 --> 00:02:08.200
You may kiss my hand."

24
00:02:08.201 --> 00:02:12.626
Her hand was smaller than the nail of my little finger.

25
00:02:12.627 --> 00:02:16.622
"I am honored to see you, Your Majesty," I replied.

26
00:02:16.623 --> 00:02:18.976
"Your palace is magnificent.

27
00:02:18.977 --> 00:02:22.898
In all my travels, I have never seen a better palace."

28
00:02:22.899 --> 00:02:26.562
I kissed her tiny hand very carefully.

29
00:02:26.563 --> 00:02:30.215
The queen and I talked for a little while.

30
00:02:30.216 --> 00:02:38.869
All things in Lilliput—the people, the birds, the animals, the plants and trees—are tiny.

31
00:02:38.870 --> 00:02:43.580
The people would fit nicely into my daughter's dollhouse.

32
00:02:43.581 --> 00:02:49.363
Even the tallest trees on the island are only a little taller than I am.

33
00:02:49.364 --> 00:02:55.238
When I first arrived, I was surprised at the smallness of everything.

34
00:02:55.239 --> 00:02:59.496
After a few weeks, though, I got used to it.

35
00:02:59.497 --> 00:03:04.159
Day by day, I learned more about the customs of Lilliput.

36
00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:10.526
In Lilliput, as in England, a person who does something bad is punished.

37
00:03:10.527 --> 00:03:15.539
The king of Lilliput, however, also rewards good people.

38
00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:20.777
If they obey all laws for six years, he gives them money.

39
00:03:20.778 --> 00:03:25.312
"What an interesting idea," I said to myself.

40
00:03:25.313 --> 00:03:29.036
"The king of England does not reward people for good behavior.

41
00:03:29.037 --> 00:03:31.677
His people might behave better if he did."

42
00:03:31.678 --> 00:03:35.320
One day, a visitor came to see me.

43
00:03:35.321 --> 00:03:38.153
"My name is Reldresal," he said.

44
00:03:38.154 --> 00:03:40.326
"I am the king's chief assistant.

45
00:03:40.327 --> 00:03:44.767
I help him make decisions and take care of his important business."

46
00:03:44.768 --> 00:03:49.164
"I am very happy to meet you, sir," I said to Reldresal.

47
00:03:49.165 --> 00:03:52.341
"Please thank His Majesty for giving me my freedom.

48
00:03:52.342 --> 00:03:55.653
Now I can explore your lovely island."

49
00:03:55.654 --> 00:04:01.043
"The king set you free," explained my new friend, "because he needs your help.

50
00:04:01.044 --> 00:04:03.120
Lilliput is in danger."

51
00:04:03.121 --> 00:04:05.860
"What kind of danger?" I asked.

52
00:04:05.861 --> 00:04:10.224
"Ah, that is a long story," Reldresal replied.

53
00:04:10.225 --> 00:04:17.157
"Let me tell you a little of the history of Lilliput."
